# Walls traced from the black (and brown, upper level) lines of Footleg's PocketTopo plan sketch;
# lines inside the passage (ledges, channel and upper-level edges) are drawn as thin borders;
# boulders as rock borders, and his slope triangles as gradient arrows;
# the invisible outline around them gives the passage fill. Water areas, water flow and
# formations come from the sketch's blue and green marks, labels from its notes. Floor steps,
# climbs and gradients come from the floor line of the extended-elevation sketch.

